# Actuary SME Review Protocol (`!actuaryreview`)

This is the always-on protocol for the **Actuary SME** review workflow.
It defines:

1. The explicit `!actuaryreview` command and its arguments.
2. The natural-language phrases that trigger the same workflow.
3. The auto-trigger conditions that fire the workflow without an
   explicit invocation.
4. The orchestration: evidence collection -> readonly subagent ->
   verdict file -> autonomous fix-and-rereview loop with safeguards.
5. The verdict storage convention.

The skill that defines the SME persona, checklist, and verdict template
is at `annuity_model/.cursor/skills/actuary-sme/SKILL.md`. The rule
here defines the orchestration; the skill defines the judgment.

---

## 1. Triggers

### 1.1 Explicit commands

When the user types one of these as a message (or as the first token
of a message), treat it as the command -- not natural language.

| Command | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `!actuaryreview` | Incremental review: diff of current work-tree vs `HEAD`. Default scope. |
| `!actuaryreview full` | Full project review across all 10 products + cross-product / documentation consistency. |
| `!actuaryreview <product>` | Focused review of one product (`spia`, `term`, `rila`, `myga`, `fia`, `va`, `wl`, `ul`, `iul`, `vul`). |
| `!actuaryreview portfolio` | Same as `!actuaryreview product:portfolio` -- multi-policy aggregation, inforce I/O, portfolio workbook. |
| `!actuaryreview status` | List the most recent verdict files under `.cursor/actuary-reviews/` (newest first, ~10 entries). Do NOT run the loop. |

### 1.2 Natural-language equivalents

If a user message contains any of the following phrases (case
insensitive, anywhere in the message), treat the message as
semantically identical to `!actuaryreview` and follow the formal
orchestration in §2. Do NOT improvise an in-line "let me just look at
that for you" review -- the artifact (verdict file under
`.cursor/actuary-reviews/`) is required in every case.

- "actuary review"
- "actuarial review"
- "actuary SME review" / "actuarial SME review"
- "have the actuary review"
- "ask the actuary"
- "review by the actuary"
- "actuary, please review" / "Actuary SME, please review"
- "do an actuary review" / "do actuary review"

If the user's phrasing also includes a scope hint -- "do a full
actuary review", "actuary review for FIA", etc. -- map it to the
matching command argument:

- "full" -> `!actuaryreview full`
- product code or display name in the message -> `!actuaryreview <code>`
  (use `portfolio` for the multi-policy runner / inforce / aggregation surface)
- otherwise -> `!actuaryreview` (incremental)

### 1.3 Auto-trigger (always-on)

Before declaring any task done that included an **edit / write** (not
a read-only inspection) to any file matching one of the following
globs in the current session, the agent MUST self-fire `!actuaryreview`
and surface the verdict before claiming task-complete.

Auto-trigger globs:

- `annuity_model/*_projection.py`
- `annuity_model/build_*_excel_workbook.py`
- `annuity_model/alm_excel_ladder.py`
- `annuity_model/excel_builder_helpers.py`
- `annuity_model/parity_constants.py`
- `annuity_model/actuarial_benchmarks.py`
- `annuity_model/account_value.py`
- `annuity_model/crediting.py`
- `annuity_model/lapse.py`
- `annuity_model/mortality_2017_cso.py`
- `annuity_model/data_registry.py`
- `annuity_model/products/*/engine.py`
- `annuity_model/products/*/excel.py`
- `annuity_model/products/*/schema.py`
- `annuity_model/liability_layouts.py`
- `annuity_model/liability_dispatch.py`
- `annuity_model/product_excel.py`
- `annuity_model/product_registry.py`
- `annuity_model/portfolio.py`
- `annuity_model/portfolio_runner.py`
- `annuity_model/liability_aggregation.py`
- `annuity_model/build_portfolio_excel_workbook.py`
- `annuity_model/inforce_io.py`
- `annuity_model/inforce_parsers.py`
- `annuity_model/products/*/inforce.py`

Read-only inspection of these files does NOT auto-fire the trigger.
The agent fires it only after at least one write to one of them.

