## 3. Verdict storage

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `.cursor/actuary-reviews/iter-<N>-<UTC>-<scope>.md` | Per-iteration verdict file. Versioned (audit trail of decisions). |
| `.cursor/actuary-reviews/_evidence-current.md` | Transient evidence pack. Overwritten each iteration. |
| `.cursor/actuary-reviews/README.md` | One-pager explaining the directory; tracked. |
| `.cursor/actuary-reviews/.gitkeep` | Keeps the dir present in git; tracked. |

Verdict files and the evidence pack are gitignored (personal session
artifacts), the same convention as `.cursor/handoffs/`. The README and
.gitkeep are tracked.

---

## 4. Operating rules

- This protocol runs only when triggered (§1). Do NOT spontaneously
  run an actuary review on every turn.
- The SME subagent is `readonly=True`. The PARENT agent applies
  fixes; the SME never edits.
- Do NOT prompt the user for the next step at any point in the loop.
  The loop is autonomous; escalations print a report, the user reads
  it when they look.
- Do NOT modify `tests/parity/golden/sme_baseline.json` from inside
  the loop. That file refreshes only via `UPDATE_GOLDEN_SME=1` after
  a deliberate methodology change reviewed by a human.
- The skill at `annuity_model/.cursor/skills/actuary-sme/SKILL.md`
  is the SME's playbook. Update it when the review checklist
  changes; do not duplicate the playbook here.
- If the agent is in a readonly mode and an `!actuaryreview` is
  requested, explain that write access is needed for the loop's fix
  step and ask the user to switch modes BEFORE entering the loop.
  This is the one allowed user prompt -- it precedes the loop, it
  is not inside it.
